are adding an if/with/try statement, you need to INDENT the block that follows, so make sure to include it in both your search and replace strings! 3. If you are wrapping code in a try statement, make sure to also add an 'except' or 'finally' block.\\nBefore every edit, please\\n1. Explain the code you want to edit and why it is causing the problem 2. Explain the edit you want to make and how it fixes the problem 3. Explain how the edit does not break existing functionality\\n\\n  signature: edit <search> <replace> [<replace-all>]\\n\\n  arguments:\\n    - search (string) [required]: the text to search for (make sure to include proper whitespace if needed)\\n    - replace (string) [required]: the text to replace the search with (make sure to include proper whitespace if needed)\\n    - replace-all (boolean) [optional]: replace all occurrences rather than the first occurrence within the displayed lines\\n\\ninsert:\\n  docstring: Insert <text> at the end of the currently opened file or after <line> if specified.\\n\\n  signature: insert <text> [<line>]\\n\\n  arguments:\\n    - text (string) [required]: the text to insert\\n    - line (integer) [optional]: the line number to insert the text as new lines after\\n\\nsubmit:\\n  docstring: submits the backported patch in /backport. Must call without --confirm first to prepare the patch.\\n  signature: submit [<confirm>]\\n  arguments:\\n    - confirm (string) [optional]: once the patch is submitted, call again with --confirm to confirm the submission.\\n\\nresetbackport:\\n  docstring: Prepares the working directory for backporting. This is a _destructive_ operation and may destroy any changes (even committed ones).\\n  signature: resetbackport\\n\\n\",\"multi_line_command_endings\":{},\"submit_command_end_name\":null,\"reset_commands\":[],\"execution_timeout\":30,\"install_timeout\":300,\"total_execution_timeout\":1800,\"max_consecutive_execution_timeouts\":3},\"history_processors\":[{\"n\":50,\"polling\":1,\"always_re